---
# Run via `make check` (alongside ansible-playbook --syntax-check).
# The tree passes the strictest profile; keep it that way.
profile: production

exclude_paths:
  - ansible/kubeconfig
  - todos/
  - docs/

# No skip_list.
#
# This used to skip var-naming[no-role-prefix]. That skip is gone: every
# registered and set_fact variable is now `__<role>_`-prefixed and every role
# default is `<role>_`-prefixed, so the rule passes on its own merits instead of
# being switched off. The reason for doing the renames rather than keeping the
# skip: site.yml runs all five node roles in ONE play, so they share a single
# variable namespace for the whole run, and `meta: flush_handlers` in
# kubernetes_node already reaches across role boundaries. "No collisions today"
# was true but fragile.
#
# The one variable intentionally NOT `__`-prefixed is
# control_plane_join_command: it is a published output of the control_plane role
# that the worker role reads via hostvars, so it is interface, not internal.
